  "id": "COMPOUND:20023 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "Juncin O is implicated in the target pathway leading to Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5 through multiple independent routes. The evidence suggests that Juncin O interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a known target of various compounds, including (+)-Phylliroside, quillaic acid, and pioglitazone. These compounds are all capable of modulating the activity of the EZH2 complex, which in turn affects the methylation of histone H3 lysine 9. The shared involvement of the EZH2 complex in the target pathways implies a potential mechanism by which Juncin O influences histone methylation, likely through the regulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The consistent presence of the EZH2 complex as a target in multiple pathways supports the idea that Juncin O may act as a modulator of this complex, thereby influencing the histone methylation process. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the EZH2 complex in mediating the effects of Juncin O on histone modification, suggesting a central role in the biological outcome.",
